  "facts": [
    "Designed by Zaha Hadid, the Danjiang Bridge showcases a single-tower asymmetric cable-stayed design, with a 200‑meter pylon supporting a 920‑meter deck that carries road, rail, and pedestrian traffic.",
    "Commissioned by the Highway Bureau, the bridge was built to link the national highway system and relieve congestion on the upstream Guandu Bridge, opening new routes for commuters.",
    "In 2015, Zaha Hadid Architects, alongside Leonhardt, Andrä & Partner and Sinotech Engineering Consultants, won the international competition that secured the bridge’s iconic design."
